<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105481" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐ-ώροφος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄροφος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of three stories</i> or <i>floors,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.180
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ορ-</span>
			), <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				6.16
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristid.
					<u>Or.</u>
					27(16).20
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.143
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πύργοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					13.8.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίστεγον</span>
			, <i>third story,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>3 Ki.</u>
				6.13(8)
			</span></i>, in pl. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐ-ώρῠγος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄργυια</span>) <i>of three fathoms,</i>
			restored in <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				6.1.52
			</span></i> by L. Dind. from the best codd. (which have <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριώρων</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριώρυον</span>), others having <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριόργὑἰ<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>: cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διώρυγος,
				πεντώρυγος.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
